UPDATE artists SET bio_en = 'Yammy —born Carmen Jamilka Peña Vargas in Yamasá, and known earlier as Yami Bonetti— is a Dominican bachata singer and songwriter based in New York who returned to the stage in 2019 under her current name after a break from her first career.

**From backing singer to «Yami Bonetti»**

According to her own biography, she began at thirteen as a backing singer in a family group and then sang in local merengue and bachata groups, playing festivals across the country. Diario Libre reported in June 2010, citing a profile in the Miami newspaper El Nuevo Herald, that at nineteen she was a former second-row singer of «Las Caribeñas» who had quit because she was tired of being placed behind the lead singers; her first album led with «No me queda más», a bachata version of a song by Selena, and included Selena’s «Como una flor». Her biography adds that her single «Ya no vives en mí» made her one of the prominent bachateras of a new generation and took her on tours of the United States and the Caribbean, and that after about four years as Yami Bonetti she stepped away from the stage to focus on her personal life.

**Back as «Yammy»**

In 2019 she returned as Yammy, adding collaborations and urban and tropical fusions to her bachata, with singles such as «Mala», «Te Superé», «Fuiste un Error», «La Gran Señora» and «El Gallo», a collaboration with Bulin 47 that has passed 1.4 million views on YouTube. She lists collaborations with Joe Veras, Luis Miguel del Amargue and El Cherry Scom, among others, and has begun writing her own songs, working with producers and songwriters including Leo RD and Cromo X. Her singles since include «Tu Dama de Hierro» (2023), «Brindo X Mi Ex» (2024) and «Te Duele Verme Bien» (2025), written with Eddie Espinal.

**Legacy**

On 5 March 2026 she appeared on «Reina de Corazones», the third volume of the «Bchta Rising» compilation series from «BCHTA Records», a collection of several bachata artists in which her song «Papi» is track two and which also includes Lady Laura. She continues to release singles and perform in the United States, and in September 2025 gave a long interview to the YouTube channel Bacharlando.' WHERE slug = 'yammy';

